DESCRIPTION:RSVP FORMPlease RSVP for this engagement opportunity or for ot
 her opportunities that work best for you. Your RSVP helps us anticipate pa
 rticipation and plan for interpretation and other available accessibility 
 supports. PPS is creating dedicated opportunities for Native and Indigeno
 us families\, students and community partners to engage in the rightsizing
  process\, learn about what is being considered\, ask questions\, and shar
 e perspectives about how potential changes may impact Native students\, fa
 milies and communities.Rightsizing engagement with Native and Indigenous c
 ommunities is coordinated by Dr. Miranda Ryan\, Director of Native Communi
 ty Engagement and Educational Partnerships\, in collaboration with the Dir
 ector of Indian Education. Together\, they are working to ensure these con
 versations are connected to the relationships\, priorities and ongoing wor
 k of PPS Indian Education and our Native community partners.
LOCATION:Barbie's Village (935 NE 33rd Ave)
SUMMARY:Community Voice: Native Families
END:VEVENT
